  "problem": "If $A={3,4,5,6,9,10,15}$ and $B={3,4,5,7},$ then $A\u2216B=$",
  "worked_solution": "The set $A\u2216B$ is the set of all elements belonging to $A$ but *not* $B.$ Note that the elements $3,4,5\\in B$ are also in $A,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\u2216B & =A-B \\\\  & ={3,4,5,6,9,10,15}-{3,4,5,7} \\\\  & ={6,9,10,15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
